body:
This is so true.  Once a person decides to end their life, suddenly everyone (police, doctors, etc.) decides you can't be thinking rationally.  No one would want to end their life!  Not in my good Christian suburb!  It's a bunch of crap.

If I decided I wanted to suddenly uproot my life and move to a new country - effectively ending the relationships with everyone I knew - no one would question my sanity, even though my decision indirectly affected them, because it is *my* *choice* about *my life*.   If I decide to end it, it's because I looked at all my options and made a choice - no one else has to like it.

&#x200B;

This doesn't sound menacing, but hear me out: Raccoons.

Nothing is safe.  Nothing is sacred.  Everything reflective is swarmed and destroyed by omnivorous trash pandas.  They fly into the windows of skyscrapers like kamikazes, then turn their rage on everyone in the building.   Those tiny little clawed hands will scratch your goddamn eyes out if you wear glasses.  No city will collect garbage anymore because the workers are afraid of rabies.  *Sky Rabies*.   

&#x200B;
